.TH TM5LINUX-CLI 1 "October 2026" "TM5 for Linux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tm5linux-cli \- RAM stability tester that runs TestMem5 (TM5) configs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tm5linux-cli
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tm5linux-cli
tests memory the way TestMem5 does: it reserves almost all free RAM, locks it, splits it between
all CPU threads and runs the test sequence of a TM5 config (by default Extreme1 by anta777) for a
number of cycles. Every value written is read back and compared bit for bit; any difference is
reported as an error.
.PP
On a terminal a live dashboard is shown. When the output is redirected, plain timestamped lines are
printed. The graphical front end is started with \fBtm5linux\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fINAME|FILE\fR
Preset name (extreme, absolut, universal2, pcbdestroyer) or path to a TM5 .cfg file.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-memory " " \fISIZE\fR
Amount of memory to test, e.g. \fB12G\fR, \fB8192M\fR or \fB90%\fR of the available memory.
Default: all available memory minus a safety reserve.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Number of worker threads (default: all CPU threads).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-cycles " " \fIN\fR
Number of cycles (default: from the config; 0 runs until stopped).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-time\-scale " " \fIPCT\fR
Scale the duration of every test (default 100).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-stop\-on\-error
Stop at the first error.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lock
Do not lock the tested memory.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hugepages
Do not request transparent huge pages.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow testing more memory than is currently available.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Use a fixed random seed.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Write the log to FILE (default: ~/.local/share/tm5linux/logs/).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-log
Do not write a log file.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list\-presets
List available configs.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-describe
Explain every test of the selected config.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-sysinfo
Show CPU, memory, memory-locking and temperature status.
.TP
.B \-\-sensors
Show the CPU and RAM (DIMM) temperatures and which kernel sensors are used. CPU temperatures come
from k10temp/zenpower (AMD), coretemp (Intel) or cpu_thermal (ARM); RAM temperatures from spd5118
(DDR5) or jc42 (DDR4) when the modules have a sensor.
.TP
.B \-\-selftest
Verify that simulated bit flips are detected.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output, one JSON object per line.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only print the final result.
.SH MEMORY LOCKING
Locking keeps the tested memory in RAM so it cannot be swapped out. It needs root or the
CAP_IPC_LOCK capability, which the installer grants with
.B setcap cap_ipc_lock=ep /usr/bin/tm5linux-cli
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TM5LINUX_SYSFS
Read sensors from this directory instead of /sys (used by the test suite).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 passed, 1 memory errors found, 2 stopped, 3 could not run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tm5linux/configs/
Your own TM5 .cfg files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tm5linux/logs/
Test logs.

